# Button press & busy feedback (UX 2026)

Users must **feel** a tap immediately. Async work often lags — never leave a primary control looking dead.

## Required for tappable primary / secondary actions

Use `Pressable` with a **pressed** style (not only `opacity` on the whole screen):

| State | Visual |
|-------|--------|
| Default | Solid fill + visible border matching the fill |
| Pressed | Darker fill + **contrasting darker/lighter border** + slight `scale: 0.97` |
| Busy (work > ~140ms) | Small `ActivityIndicator` in the button + short label like `Working…`; disable double-taps |

### Patterns (Healthings palette)

- **Sky Next** (`#5BAFE8`): pressed → deeper blue + navy border
- **Navy CTA** (`#1A2B4A`): pressed → near-black navy + sky border
- **Ghost / Back**: pressed → navy border + light navy wash background

```tsx
<Pressable
  style={({ pressed }) => [
    styles.btn,
    pressed && !busy && styles.btnPressed,
    busy && styles.btnDisabled,
  ]}
  disabled={busy}
  onPress={() => void onPressAsync()}
>
  {showSpinner ? <ActivityIndicator color="#fff" size="small" /> : null}
  <Text>{showSpinner ? 'Working…' : 'Label'}</Text>
</Pressable>
```

Delay the spinner ~120–160ms so fast actions do not flash.

## Do not

- Rely on default Pressable with no pressed style
- Block the UI with no in-button feedback while `await`ing save/sync/OAuth
- Use green for new chrome CTAs — navy / sky blue (see Quick Start)

